<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="bacnet-NetworkPort" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">Network ports (bacnet-NetworkPort)</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">These components send and receive messages to and from
the BACnet link layer. All BACnet networks support these ports: <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">IpPort</uicontrol> and <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">EthernetPort</uicontrol>. The <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">MstpPort</uicontrol> works only in a remote controller and is available
only in the <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname> module/palette. In addition,
network ports include the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">ScPort</uicontrol> and <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">SCHubPort</uicontrol>.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">network port</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">IpPort</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">EthernetPort</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">MstpPort</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">ports</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section "><p class="- topic/p ">Each port supports the same port-level properties, including <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Poll Service</parmname>, <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Port Id</parmname>, <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Port Info</parmname>. Each provides a unique set of <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Link</uicontrol> properties.</p><fig id="ID-fig-00000008" class="- topic/fig "><title id="ID-00000099" class="- topic/title ">Example: Ethernet Port properties, Link container
expanded</title><image placement="break" scale="65" width="700" href="../graphic/network_ipPort.png" class="- topic/image "/></fig><p class="- topic/p ">You access these properties by expanding <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetNetwork</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Bacnet Comm</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Network</uicontrol></menucascade> followed by double-clicking the
port node.</p><p class="- topic/p ">If needed, add a port from the <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname>, <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnetAws</apiname> or <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnetOws</apiname> palettes.
Each port container communicates based on the type of port (Ip, Ethernet,
MS/TP, etc). The <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname> module supports up to 4
MS/TP ports, depending on the host platform, as well as licensing
considerations.</p><p class="- topic/p ">In addition to the common properties (Status,
Fault Cause and Enabled), this component has these properties.</p></section><properties class="- topic/simpletable reference/properties "><prophead class="- topic/sthead      reference/prophead "><proptypehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptypehd ">Property</proptypehd><propvaluehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvaluehd ">Value</propvaluehd><propdeschd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdeschd ">Description</propdeschd></prophead><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Network Number</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">number from 1-65534 (defaults to 0)</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Serves as a unique identifier for each BACnet network. This is crucial in large systems where multiple BACnet networks may coexist. Each device within a BACnet network must have its network number defined to facilitate communication. You cannot enable the network port if the network number is invalid.  If the network port is enabled, the network number cannot be changed to an invalid value.</propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Network Number Quality</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only (defaults to <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Unknown</systemoutput>)</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Provides information regarding the state of the network number assigned to a specific port. <ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">It displays <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Unknown</systemoutput> when a BNetworkPort is first added to the station and the network number is set to -1.</p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "> If the Network Number is set through <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword "/> or BACnet, it displays <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Configured</systemoutput>. </p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "> If a NetworkNumberIs message is received by the station and the Network Number Quality is <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Unknown</systemoutput> or <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Learned</systemoutput>, the Network Number will be updated and the Network Number Quality updated to <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Learned</systemoutput> or <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Learned Configured</systemoutput>. </p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">NetworkNumberIs messages are ignored if the Network Number Quality is <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Learned Configured</systemoutput> or <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Configured</systemoutput>.  </p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">The Network Number Quality will be set back to <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">Unknown</systemoutput> if the Network Number is set to zero or -1.</p></li></ul></propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Link</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">additional properties</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Configures the Ethernet connection. A separate topic documents
these properties.</propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Poll Service</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">additional properties</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Contains network polling properties. A separate topic documents
these properties.</propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Max Devices</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Indicates maximum devices available in the network.</propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Port Id</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc "><div conkeyref="reusekey/bacnetPortId-div" class="- topic/div "/></propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Port Info</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc "><div conkeyref="bacnet/bacnetPortInfo-div" class="- topic/div "/></propdesc></property></properties><section class="- topic/section "><title class="- topic/title ">Actions</title><ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Enable</uicontrol> activates the port.</p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Disable</uicontrol> deactivates the port.</p></li></ul></section></refbody></reference>